From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:02:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 161/161] hjviewer: hjv-e2e builds delete the login's account
 from the command line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1.9.1's E2E (DEL1-DEL3) deletes accounts through the client's own signed
request. --hjv-e2e-delete-account sends [계정 삭제]'s POST
/api/hjv/account/delete with the confirmation's fixed body as http_request
does: signed by the account hook H13, its answer observed by H14, which
logs the device out on "deleted":true. With "again" the very same bytes go
once more, as http_request_sync's own second try sends them, so that the
E2E sees hjv-api answer a retry with the first answer. It prints each
answer's status and body and whether the login's values were kept, never
the values. Only in builds with the hjv-e2e feature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hjviewer_e2e.rs | 68 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 68 insertions(+)

